      "message": "@ssundher@google.com we further looked into your suggestion. With the additional suggestions from your colleagues to include also Build.VERSION.SDK_INT \u003c\u003d Build.VERSION_CODES.VANILLA_ICE_CREAM it gets complicated using RequiredProperties:\n\nIf we want to put the condition isAutomotive \u0026\u0026 Build.VERSION.SDK_INT \u003c\u003d Build.VERSION_CODES.VANILLA_ICE_CREAM as a @RequiredProperties , we would need to combine it into a single property - e.g.: NOT_AUTMOTIVE_AND_NOT_BUILD_VERSION_VANILLA_ICE_CREAM_OR_LOWER . RequiredProperties are evaluated such that every required property needs to be true - meaning splitting it up in 2 RequiredProperties (i.e. @RequiredProperties({NOT_AUTMOTIVE, NOT_BUILD_VERSION_VANILLA_ICE_CREAM_OR_OLDER}) is not equivalent to NOT_AUTMOTIVE_AND_NOT_BUILD_VERSION_VANILLA_ICE_CREAM_OR_LOWER (\u003d: isAutomotive \u0026\u0026 Build.VERSION.SDK_INT \u003c\u003d Build.VERSION_CODES.VANILLA_ICE_CREAM ). So implementing NOT_AUTMOTIVE_AND_NOT_BUILD_VERSION_VANILLA_ICE_CREAM_OR_LOWER is the only option of we want to use RequiredProperties.\n\nSudheer, should we a.) implement RequiredProperties({NOT_AUTMOTIVE_AND_NOT_BUILD_VERSION_VANILLA_ICE_CREAM_OR_LOWER}) or should we b.) proceed with the current approach of assumeFalse(isAutomotive() \u0026\u0026 Build.VERSION.SDK_INT \u003c\u003d Build.VERSION_CODES.VANILLA_ICE_CREAM ) ?",
